       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change my concern, for two reasons:\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make that safe. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm.\n2. **The confirmation didn't come from a prescriber.** You told me you aren't a clinician, and you haven't said the treating prescriber approved this dose. An unusual order like this needs sign-off from the treating physician or pharmacist.\n\nYou have a few ways to move forward:\n- Ask the treating prescriber to place or confirm the order. If they intend a dose above the labeled maximum, they can enter it directly and document the reason, and pharmacy can review it.\n- Give me a dose within the labeled range, such as 800 mg PO four times daily or 600 mg PO every 6 hours, and I'll enter it.\n- Tell me what the order is for, such as pain, fever, or inflammation. Then the prescriber can pick the right drug and dose.\n\nIf a clinician gives me a revised order, I can enter it right away."
      }
